{title: 254 - The Great Physician Now is Near}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #254 • SYMPATHY • 8.7.8.7.}
{lyricist: William Hunter}
{composer: J. H. Stockton}
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 254}
{meta: tune SYMPATHY}
{meta: meter 8.7.8.7.}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db/Ab]The great Physician now is [Ab]near,
[Ab]The sympathizing [Ab7]Jesus;
[Ab7]He speaks the drooping [Db/Ab]heart to cheer,
[Db/F]O hear the voice of Jesus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Db/Ab]Sweetest note in seraph song,
[Ab]Sweetest name on mortal tongue;
[Ab7]Sweetest carol ever sung,
[Ab7]Jesus, blessed Jesus.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db/Ab]Your many sins are all forgiven,
[Ab]Oh! hear the [Ab7]voice of Jesus;
[Ab7]Go on your way [Db/F]in peace to heaven,
[Db/F]And wear a crown with Jesus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db/Ab]All glory to the dying [Ab]Lamb!
[Ab]I now believe [Ab7]in Jesus;
[Ab7]I love the [Db/F]blessed Savior's name,
[Db/F]I love the name of Jesus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Db/Ab]His name dispels my guilt and [Ab]fear,
[Ab]No other [Ab7]name but Jesus;
[Ab7]Oh! how my soul [Db/F]delights to hear
[Db/F]The charming name of Jesus.
{end_of_verse}
